  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 127 PM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nCold front is located from NW Lower MI to NW Illinois with\ncoldest air lagging somewhat behind. Area of weak lift ahead of\nthe front was allowing for some patchy drizzle or very light \nshowers. Questions remain as to timing of the front and arrival\nof colder temps and upper level/sfc troughs that will aid in\nlake effect development. Models vary anywhere from 00Z Fri to 3Z\nFri for fropa in the NW and taking several hours to work \nacross. Greatest pops should focus either side of the front \nwhere forcing is strongest with a return to lesser coverage \n(possibly brief end) to showers. Have tried to capture in pops \nas best as possible. The larger challenge comes with transition \nfrom a lake enhanced setup to pure lake effect. Original signals\nwere closer to 12Z Fri, but signs seem to suggest this could be\ndelayed by at least a few hours as we await some of the \nstronger troughs. Still appears to be a window for 1 or 2 single\nbands at the peak of the event Friday afternoon. Have also made\nsome changes with regards to timing and position, but \nconfidence is on the lower side on exact evolution. Precip will \nbe in the form of rain, and as mentioned by the mid forecaster \nsome pretty stout instability could materialize resulting in \nlocalized heavier rain amounts and maybe a bit of graupel if \nsufficient height can be obtained. Away from the lake, dry \nconditions should settle in several hours behind the front. \nCan't rule out some sprinkles or light showers with the passage \nof each trough, but moisture will be more limited. Temperatures \nwill be noticeably cooler with highs in the 50s and lows in the \n30s heading into the weekend. \n\nNo changes in the latter period as high pressure will dominate\ninto mid week. Pattern suggests we could be on the edge of a\nmore active flow with shower chances mid to late week.",
